.git
# Development tooling and local state; nothing an image builds from.
bin
dist
web/node_modules
web/**/node_modules
web/**/dist

# The two directories internal/webui embeds from.
#
# They are build output, and they are excluded so that the ONLY thing that can put
# a frontend into an image is the node stage inside the Dockerfile. Without these
# two lines, `COPY . .` would carry whichever of two wrong things happened to be on
# the builder's disk: the committed `.gitkeep` placeholder that exists so a fresh
# clone compiles, or a workstation's stale `pnpm build` output from three weeks ago.
# Both produce an image that looks built and serves something nobody chose.
#
# The failure mode this buys is the good one. With the directories absent from the
# context, the node stage's `COPY --from` is what creates them — so a broken copy
# leaves `//go:embed all:portal-dist` with no directory at all, and the build stops
# at compile time instead of shipping a control plane whose UI is a placeholder.
internal/webui/portal-dist
internal/webui/admin-dist
